<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Boussouma</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1896 CE (approx.) · capital Boussouma</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Mossi kingdom east of Ouagadougou, one of the smaller independent Mossi states of the Burkina Faso plateau.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Known mainly from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mossi">Mossi</a> oral tradition. Boussouma was founded by a branch of the Mossi royal family, probably in the 17th century, on lands east of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ouagadougou">Kingdom of Ouagadougou</a>, and its rulers bore the title Dima.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Dima of Boussouma ruled with ministers and village chiefs over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mossi">Mossi</a> farming communities, with local earth-priests keeping the rites of land. The kingdom kept its independence from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ouagadougou">Ouagadougou</a> and was a frequent rival of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mogho-naba">Mogho Naaba</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Boussouma came under French control in 1896 and became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/french-west-africa">French West Africa</a>, later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-upper-volta">French Upper Volta</a>. The Dima of Boussouma remains a traditional ruler in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burkina-faso">Burkina Faso</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1600 CE – 1896 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.54%;width:5.89%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1896 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Boussouma</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Mossi traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Moore</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/burkina-faso">Burkina Faso</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Boussouma</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1748&amp;focus=kingdom-of-boussouma" aria-label="Kingdom of Boussouma on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4650 1697 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Boussouma lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4970 1953L4958 1973M4970 1953L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4958 1973h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4970 1953h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4970 1953h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Boussouma. <a href="/atlas?year=1748&amp;focus=kingdom-of-boussouma">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

